// A <- binding is change-triggered: it re-evaluates when an input changes. But
// its input here (Y) is set once at declaration and never changes, so without a
// startup seed the binding would never fire and X would stay 0. The seed cycle
// forces every <- to fire once, so X gets its initial value Y+1 = 8 and then
// stays there (Y never changes -> no further firing). Runs in BOTH modes.
#variable Y integer = 7
#variable X integer = 0

X <- Y + 1
